{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementLP","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.ConfinementLP","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.BorromeanUnique","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramIndefinite"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.braid_coefficients_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.braid_coefficients_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementLP.lean#L100-L116","doc":"Braid words of length L produce NF coefficients bounded by (1+|HA|)^L.\nThe LP optimum requires unbounded coefficients, hence is not realizable.\n\nThis is the growth-rate argument: braid words grow polynomially in the\nNF basis (each multiplication by σ_i at most doubles degree + adds HA),\nwhile the LP optimum is at the boundary of the feasible cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lp_achieves_zero_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lp_achieves_zero_trace","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementLP.lean#L82-L96","doc":"The LP over continuous H₃(q) can achieve trace = 0.\nFollows from `gram_indefinite`: the negative eigenvalue direction\nallows trace cancellation.\n\nThe formal existential statement requires defining the LP\nfeasible set over ℝ (not R_q) with positivity constraints. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:confinement-lp","label":"prop:confinement-lp","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/confinement-lp.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.gram_indefinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.gram_indefinite","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementLP.lean#L67-L80","doc":"The Gram matrix G of H₃(q) is NOT positive definite for q > 1.\n\nProved via `gram_indefinite_witness` in GramIndefinite.lean:\nL₊² + L₋² ≠ 2·L₊·L₋ in the standard 2×2 representation,\nwhich means the Gram form has a negative eigenvalue on the\nL₊ − L₋ direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovTraceNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovTraceNF","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementLP.lean#L27-L42","doc":"The Markov trace of the NF basis elements of H₃(q).\nIndexed by Fin 6 = {γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻}.\n\ntr_M(γ)  = 1\ntr_M(σ₀) = z        where z = 1/(q^½ + q^{-½})\ntr_M(σ₁) = z\ntr_M(L₊) = z²\ntr_M(L₋) = z²\ntr_M(e⁻) = HA·z² + z ","signatureChunk":0}]}